==English==

===Etymology===
From {{w|Epsom Derby}} horse race, {{named-after|en|Edward Smith-Stanley, 12th Earl of Derby|wplink==|nocap=1}}. Ultimately from [[Derby]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɑː.bi/|a=UK,Australia}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-derby.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑː(ɹ)bi|s=2}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɝ.bi/|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)bi|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several [[annual]] [[horse race]]s.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Any organized [[race]].
#: {{ux|en|a donkey '''derby'''}}
# {{lb|en|US}} A [[bowler hat]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1906|author=O. Henry|title=s:The Green Door
|passage=He began to fan her with his hat. That was successful, for he struck her nose with the brim of his '''derby''' and she opened her eyes.}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[sport|sports]] [[match]] between [[rival]] [[team|teams]].
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[local derby]].
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=April 15, 2011
|author=Saj Chowdhury
|title=Norwich 2 - 1 Nott'm Forest
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/13009332.stm
|page=
|passage=Defeat sees Forest remain a point outside the top six with a '''derby''' against Leicester up next.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=7 March 2021|work=The Guardian|author=David Hytner|title=Manchester United catch City cold as Fernandes and Shaw end winning run|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/mar/07/manchester-city-manchester-united-premier-league-match-report|passage=The left-back had been a selection concern because of an injury niggle but his first goal since last March swung this '''derby''' decisively in United’s favour, extending their club record unbeaten run away from home in the Premier League to 22 games and torpedoing City’s sequence of 21 straight wins in all competitions.}}

